    "summary": "Laila&#039;s resting camel; single-page illustration on an album folio. Camel rests, on all fours, with a cushioned seat tied on top. A loose chain hangs from the camel&#039;s face. Inscribed. Album contains 44 paintings and drawings, mostly of Persian costumes and animals with some drawings by Kaempfer.\r\nInk and opaque watercolour on paper. Album is bound in brown leather with gold gilt  decoration. Inside covers have marbled paper.",
